 "notes": "Manual, every example app in the repo (one Hono app per folder, so routes of different apps share keys — multi-app-repo; expected = the union). Right: plain app.get/post on new Hono(). Misses and errors: new Hono() is not recognised as the application, so the roots app.get('/') are dropped (app-not-recognized); sub-apps mounted in the same file — app.route('/book', book), new Hono().basePath('/api') — lose the prefix (mount-same-scope); the blog's router is named api and taken for an HTTP client (client-named-router); the stytch TodoAPI chain is mounted with .route('/api', TodoAPI) in another file (prefix-other-file); Hono's inline regex constraint /post/:id{[0-9]+} is normalized into /post/{id}{[0-9]+} (route-constraint-syntax). No license file in the repo; only measured locally. Since H2b's TS cross-file mount graph (2026-10-16): routes chained on the constructor (export const TodoAPI = new Hono<..>().get(..).post(..)) belong to the name the chain is bound to, and a router typed with generics (new Hono<{ Bindings }>()) is one — the stytch TodoAPI under /api and the blog's api router come out right.",
